  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is negative (sentiment < 0) to account for bearish market pressure.",
    "Reduce forecast peaks by 5-10% after a spike to prevent overshoot and align with mean reversion tendencies.",
    "Apply a lag correction: if true outcome is lower than forecast, reduce next period’s forecast by 3-5% to reflect delayed market reaction.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent low prices when sentiment is neutral or slightly positive, to anticipate mean reversion.",
    "When sentiment is positive (sentiment > 0), slightly increase forecast by 2-5% to capture bullish momentum, but cap at 10% above recent high.",
    "If true outcome is consistently below forecast over 3+ consecutive days, apply a downward bias correction of 3-7% for the next 5 days."
  ]
}
